Based on my analysis, the savepoint name is a user-controllable identifier (an app developer supplies it via `transaction.savepoint("...")` or `transaction.rollback_to("...")`). The new `Savepoint` class and the `savepoint`/`rollback_to` methods interpolate this name directly into raw SQL via f-strings with no parameter binding and no allowlist, then execute it. This is a classic identifier-injection (CWE-89) in newly added code.

